<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7647" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cētus</span></b> , i, m.
		(acc. to the Gr. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cētŏs</span></b> , n., <i><span class="en">Plin. 32, 1, 4,
			§ 10</span></i>; and hence common in the plur.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cētē</span></b>  = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κήτη</span>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 5,
		822</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 24, 40, § 78</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 50, 74, § 157</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">Sil. 7,
			476</span></i>), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῆτος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>any large
			sea-animal</i>, <i>a seamonster;</i> particularly <i>a species of whale</i>, <i>a
			shark</i>, <i>dog-fish</i>, <i>seal</i>, <i>dolphin</i>, etc., Plin. l. l.; <i><span class="en">Plaut. Aul.
				2, 8, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Capt. 4, 2, 72</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cels. 2,
			18</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			As a constellation, <i>the Whale</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 9,
			7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Manil. 1, 612</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
